        ],
        "params": {
          "text": "**CT08 \u2014 Can a lead network improve settling without changing DC gain?**  \n**Predict \u2192 Run \u2192 Inspect \u2192 Change the zero. Run 64 s at 10 Hz.** P gain 4 and lead C(z)=16(z\u22120.8)/(z\u22120.2) both have DC gain 4.  \nCompare output settling and initial command: lead demands 8, P demands 2 for a 0.5 step. No actuator limiter is present. The separate pulse path measures the lead open loop; Bode gain reference must be 1.  \nSelect zero, F4: value 0.8 \u2192 0.2; save/reopen/rerun. Exact cancellation makes this controller P gain 16, not P gain 4. Plotted signals use normalized unit 1; sample n is observed at Scope time (n+1)/10 s.  \n[Open CT08 student lab](qrc:/s7studio/help/education/labs/CT08-lead-lag/README.md) \u00b7 [MIT lead compensation](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/16-06-principles-of-automatic-control-fall-2012/resources/mit16_06f12_lecture_25/) \u00b7 [MIT lag compensation](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/16-06-principles-of-automatic-control-fall-2012/resources/mit16_06f12_lecture_14/)",
          "text_format": "markdown",
